# https://github.com/browserslist/browserslist#readme
#
# Dynamic UI 2.x targets.
#
# The floor is set by ONE feature: `<dialog>.showModal()`. `DModal`,
# `DOffcanvas` and the confirm modal are native dialogs, and `showModal()` is
# what supplies the focus trap, the page inertness a screen reader needs, Escape
# and the top layer. A browser without it does not get a degraded modal — it
# gets an element it does not recognise.
#
#   dialog.showModal()   Chrome 37, Edge 79, Firefox 98, Safari 15.4
#
# Two further features the panels use degrade cleanly and so do NOT set the
# floor — without them a panel simply appears and disappears with no transition:
#
#   transition-behavior: allow-discrete   Chrome 117, Firefox 129, Safari 17.4
#   @starting-style                       Chrome 117, Firefox 129, Safari 17.5
#
# Raising the floor from the previous list (Chrome 60 / Firefox 60 / Safari 12,
# 2017–2018) is a deliberate, announced change — see the CHANGELOG. Those
# versions predate `<dialog>` entirely.

Chrome >= 100
Edge >= 100
Firefox >= 98
Safari >= 15.4
iOS >= 15.4
Samsung >= 16
Opera >= 86
not dead
